RELATIONAL CONSTANT SUBSYSTEM
Typed SID modes, PED channels, RDG operator classes
===================================================

CONSTANT CLASSES
----------------
Classify constants by the *kind of operator* that generates them:

  Phase constants:        π, τ, i
  Exponential constants:  e, ln2
  Self-similar constants: φ, √2
  Asymptotic constants:   γ, ζ(3), G
  Scaling constants:      δ
  Distribution constants: K₀, K, C₂

Each class receives a SID mode, a PED channel, and an RDG operator type.

SID MODE ASSIGNMENTS
--------------------
SID.S (Structure):
  - φ, √2        (fixed-point, metric, similarity)
  - e, ln2       (exponential structure)
  - π, τ         (geometric/rotational structure)

SID.I (Interaction):
  - i            (complex rotation generator)
  - δ            (renormalization interaction)
  - γ            (harmonic/logarithmic correction interaction)

SID.D (Dynamics):
  - ζ(3), G      (Dirichlet/analytic dynamics)
  - K₀, K, C₂    (number-theoretic distribution dynamics)

PED CHANNEL ASSIGNMENTS
-----------------------
PED.Power (P-channel):
  - e, ln2       (scaling power, compounding)
  - φ, √2        (self-similar power)
  - δ            (bifurcation scaling power)

PED.Evaluation (E-channel):
  - γ            (harmonic/logarithmic evaluation)
  - ζ(3), G      (Dirichlet evaluation)
  - K₀, K, C₂    (statistical/arithmetic evaluation)

PED.Dynamics (Q-slice):
  - π, τ, i      (phase/circulation dynamics)
  - δ            (period-doubling dynamics)
  - ζ(3), G      (analytic continuation dynamics)

RDG OPERATOR CLASSES
--------------------
PhaseOp:
  - π, τ, i
  Generates rotation, circulation, periodicity.

LinMap:
  - e, ln2
  Generates exponential flow, compounding, scaling.

SimOp:
  - φ, √2
  Generates similarity transforms, fixed-point maps.

AsympOp:
  - γ
  Generates asymptotic corrections, harmonic/log gaps.

DirichletOp:
  - ζ(3), G
  Generates Dirichlet-type analytic flux.

RenormOp:
  - δ
  Generates universal scaling under renormalization.

DistribOp:
  - K₀, K, C₂
  Generates statistical/arithmetic distribution flux.

COUPLING RULES
--------------
Given a constant c:

  SID(c) × PED(c) → RDG(c) × value(c)

Examples:

  (SID.S, PED.Dynamics) → (PhaseOp, π)
  (SID.S, PED.Power)    → (LinMap, e)
  (SID.S, PED.Power)    → (SimOp, φ)
  (SID.I, PED.Eval)     → (AsympOp, γ)
  (SID.D, PED.Eval)     → (DirichletOp, ζ(3))
  (SID.D, PED.Eval)     → (DistribOp, C₂)
  (SID.I, PED.Dynamics) → (RenormOp, δ)

EXECUTION SEMANTICS
-------------------
Each constant becomes a *typed operator*:

  π: PhaseOp → rotation by π
  τ: PhaseOp → full-cycle rotation
  i: PhaseOp → quarter-turn rotor

  e: LinMap → exponential scaling
  ln2: LinMap → binary entropy scaling

  φ: SimOp → similarity fixed point
  √2: SimOp → metric scaling

  γ: AsympOp → harmonic/log correction
  ζ(3): DirichletOp → analytic flux
  G: DirichletOp → alternating Dirichlet flux

  δ: RenormOp → universal scaling ratio

  K₀: DistribOp → CF digit distribution
  K: DistribOp → sum-of-squares distribution
  C₂: DistribOp → prime-gap distribution


FULL CONSTANT SUBSYSTEM SUMMARY
-------------------------------
For each constant c:

  c ∈ ConstantSet
  SID_Mode_Assignment(c) ∈ {S, I, D}
  PED_Channel_Assignment(c) ∈ {P, E, Q}
  RDG_Operator_Assignment(c) ∈ {
      PhaseOp, LinMap, SimOp,
      AsympOp, DirichletOp, RenormOp, DistribOp
  }

  RepresentationSet R(c) = {series, product, integral, limit, ...}
  EvalFunctional: R(c) → ℝ
  Coupling: SID(c) × PED(c) → RDG(c) × EvalFunctional(R(c))


